From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:43:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: after a revert to the minimum, the area is the cells' as
 they are
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

revertToMinCongestion() puts the cells back at the sizes of the
routability pass that measured the least congestion, and the target
density, fillers and net weights with them. It left the standard-cell
area, which only updateAreas() computes, as it was: the sum of the
sizes the cells had just left. Every way out of the routability loop
that reverts leaves it so:

- GPL-0053, GPL-0091 and GPL-0054 return before routability()'s
  updateAreas() loop and keep the sum from before the last pass
  inflated;
- GPL-0097 runs that loop and then reverts, and keeps the last pass's
  inflated sum;
- a divergence recovery (GPL-0112) reverts between passes.

The bins measure the reverted cells, since the revert ends in
updateDensitySize(), but getOverflowDenominator() divides by the stale
area. From the revert on, every overflow reads off by the ratio of the
two areas, and with it the wirelength coefficient, the timing-driven
thresholds, the convergence test and the GPL-1002 and GPL-1014
reports. On XiangShan's XSTile parent the two areas were 279,365 and
259,295 um^2, a ratio of 1.077: it converged at a reported overflow of
0.0980 that was 0.106, and GPL-1014 reported +7.74 % of area with no
inflation left.

revertToMinCongestion() now calls updateAreas() and sets the movable
area from the white space and the restored target density, as
cutFillerCells() does, before updateDensitySize().

What changes: every placement whose routability phase reverts to its
minimum, from the revert on. Placements with no pass, or whose passes
meet the congestion target (GPL-0090), do not revert and do not change.

RevertToMinimumTest.MeasuresOverflowOnTheCellsAsTheyAre, in the new
routability_minimum_test, drives the real controller on gcd in the
main loop's order (routabilitySnapshot(), runRoutability(),
isConverged()), with friend access standing in for the Nesterov steps
between the passes. Its minimum is pass 2, and the phase ends through
GPL-0054 in one case and GPL-0097 in the other. Without the change the
standard-cell area is that of the sizes the cells left (+14 % and +8 %),
and so is the overflow's denominator.

No compared regression golden prints a revert: simple01-rd to
simple04-rd run one pass that ends in GPL-0090. Of the pass/fail tests
that run routability, upf_aes changes: its phase ends through GPL-0097
with its minimum at pass 9 of 10. GPL-1014 now reports +25.71 %, the
inflation GPL-1012 reports, instead of +30.00 % for the sizes of pass
10; the top region converges one iteration sooner at a final weighted
congestion of 1.0500 instead of 1.0678, and HPWL is +0.06 %.
place_ios_rd goes back to its minimum through GPL-0054, after passes
that inflated nothing, and its log is byte-identical, as are
congestion_inflation_default's and place_ios_td's.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
